{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Listen</b> Above it is written: \"Write this song,\" and adjacent to it is האזינו. Just as you listened and heard the words of Torah, so listen to the words of this song. According to the plain sense, האזינו השמים — meaning: dwellers of great cities and fortresses in the heavens." "<b>And let the earth hear</b> — dwellers of the earth. Meaning: dwellers of villages and small towns." "<b>The heavens and I will speak</b> — totals תרי\"ג. That is: listen for תרי\"ג commandments. The verse begins with ה\"א and ends with יו\"ד, including the Name at the head of the song. And it has 7 words, and this is \"חצבה עמודיה שבעה\" — corresponding to 7 firmaments, and 7 lands, and 7 days of creation." "<b>ותשמע</b> — twice in the Masorah. This one, and the other: ותשמע ותושיע. If you hear the words of My mouth, you will be saved — and this is ותשמע ותושיע."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:13.655787512Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}